{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מי מנה עפר יעקב", :translit "mi manah afar ya'akov", :gloss "who has counted the dust of Jacob"} {:he "עופר האילים", :translit "ofer ha-ayyalim", :gloss "the young of the hinds"} {:he "כי נער ישראל ואהבהו", :translit "ki na'ar yisra'el va'ohavohu", :gloss "for Israel is a youth and I loved him"} {:he "מן יכול לממני דעדקיא דבית יעקב", :translit "min y'khul l'mimnei d'adya d'veit ya'akov", :gloss "who could count the multitudes of the house of Jacob"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking עפר (dust) to עופר (young hind) based on Hosea 11:1 where Israel is called נער (youth); Onkelos renders עפר as עדקיא (multitudes), supporting this reading."}], :frame {:text "The word עפר (dust) in Numbers 23:10 is read as an allusion to עופר האילים, the young of hinds, because Hosea 11:1 calls Israel נער (a youth) whom God loves. Onkelos on this verse translates עפר as עדקיא (multitudes), reading not literal dust but countless offspring.", :sources ["Hosea 11:1" "Onkelos on Numbers 23:10"]}} {:quotes [{:he "עפר", :translit "afar", :gloss "dust"} {:he "ערלה", :translit "arlah", :gloss "foreskin"} {:he "עדלה", :translit "adlah", :gloss "the boy's first urine after circumcision"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "עפר", :b "ערלה בחול"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "תמות", :translit "tamut", :gloss "let me die / he dies"} {:he "תמות נפשי עם פלשתים", :translit "tamut nafshi im plishtim", :gloss "let my soul die with the Philistines"} {:he "תמות בנוער נפשם", :translit "tamut b'no'ar nafsham", :gloss "their soul dies in youth"} {:he "אנשי דמים ומרמה לא יחצו ימיהם", :translit "anshei damim u'mirmah lo yach'tzu y'meihem", :gloss "men of blood and deceit shall not halve their days"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["תמות" "תמות נפשי עם פלשתים" "תמות בנוער נפשם"]}], :frame {:text "Balaam asked to die the death of the upright (Numbers 23:10), but he instead met the fate described by the other two occurrences of תמות: he died the death of the wicked, like Samson's plea to die with the Philistines (Judges 16:30), and his life was cut short in youth, as Psalm 55:24 states that men of blood and deceit shall not halve their days. Balaam was killed by the Israelites at thirty-four years old.", :sources ["Judges 16:30" "Psalm 55:24" "Numbers 31:8"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ישרים", :translit "y'sharim", :gloss "the upright"} {:he "אבות העולם", :translit "avot ha-olam", :gloss "the fathers of the world"} {:he "בלעם", :translit "bil'am", :gloss "Balaam"} {:he "ותהי אחריתי כמוהו", :translit "v't'hi achariti k'mohu", :gloss "and let my end be like his"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ישרים", :b "אבות העולם"} {:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "אברהם יצחק יעקב", :spells "םקם"} {:kind :gematria, :a "םקם", :b "בלעם"} {:kind :other, :note "Numbers 24:14 phrase 'ותהי אחריתי כמוהו' (my end shall be like his) links Balaam's end to the patriarchs."}], :frame {:text "Balaam said in Numbers 24:14, 'I will advise you what this people shall do to your people in the end of days.' The rabbis identify Balaam with the wicked, in contrast to the patriarchs whom Balaam wished to emulate. The phrase 'and let my end be like his' in Numbers 24:14 is understood as Balaam desiring to share the destiny of Israel.", :sources ["Numbers 24:14"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking עפר (dust) to עופר (young hind) based on Hosea 11:1 where Israel is called נער (youth); Onkelos renders עפר as עדקיא (multitudes), supporting this reading.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:a-value 350, :b-value 351, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "ערלה בחול", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "עפר"} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["תמות" "תמות נפשי עם פלשתים" "תמות בנוער נפשם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "תמות", :refs ["Genesis 2:17" "Genesis 20:7" "Exodus 7:18" "Exodus 10:28" "Judges 6:23" "Judges 16:30" "1 Samuel 14:44" "1 Samuel 20:2"], :n 34, :lens :exact} {:phrase "תמות נפשי עם פל